From 5c9ffb675d08add8cef83de096be71fdb7ce45ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] cryptonote_core: check a block's key-image domains over
 the compute pool

Why: check_tx_semantic checks that each key image is not the identity and
is in the prime-order subgroup, one scalar multiplication per key image, on
the block thread. For a block of about 1,300 one-input transactions that is
about 0.12 s on a Ryzen 9 3900X core and about 0.45 s on a Core 2 Quad.

For 8 or more transactions, ver_non_input_consensus now passes
skip_keyimages_domain to check_tx_semantic, collects the key images, and
checks them all after the loop with ver_keyimages_domain_batch, in chunks of
at least 32 over the pool, with the same failure flags (verification
failed, invalid input). Fewer transactions, and every other caller of
check_tx_semantic, take the original path.

Safety:
- The test per key image is check_tx_inputs_keyimages_domain's. A
  transaction whose key images fail is still rejected, and so is the block.
- A key image that does not decode used to throw out of check_tx_semantic;
  in the batch it fails the check. Both reject.
- Only the order of checks that each reject changes: a key-image failure is
  now found after the other per-transaction rules of the batch.
- Verification only; public data.

Tests: tx_verification_utils.keyimages_domain_batch (200 valid key images;
none; a torsion component at 0, 99 and 199, in the batch and alone; the
identity; a key image that does not decode).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
